{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-40170"
  ],
  "description": "Zou Dikai discovered that ngtcp2 serialized peer transport parameters into\na fixed 1024-byte stack buffer without bounds checking. When qlog was\nenabled, a remote attacker could possibly use this issue to execute\narbitrary code.",
  "id": "USN-8300-1",
  "isummary": "ngtcp2 could be made to run programs as your login if it received specially\ncrafted network traffic when qlog was enabled.",
